== About me
I am a postdoctoral fellow in the Department of Statistics at Harvard University, working with Professor [http://people.seas.harvard.edu/~samurphy/ Susan Murphy]. I received my Ph.D. in Biostatistics and Health Data Science from the Duke-National University of Singapore Medical School, where I was advised by Professor [https://blog.nus.edu.sg/bibhas/ Bibhas Chakraborty]. Earlier, I earned my Master's degree in Biostatistics and Bachelor's degree in Medicine and Applied Mathematics from Peking University.

== Research Interest
I develop statistical and machine learning methods for impactful applications in digital health. My primary research interests include:

    - Contextual bandits and Reinforcement learning
    - Longitudinal data analysis and Causal Inference
    - Design and analysis of experiments
    - Just-in-time adaptive intervention



